silm:instances_papers_16_one_integrated_growing_knowledge_graph_chapters_04_yoneda_for_integration_sections_01_integrated_representable_concrete_anchors#integratedrepresentablecrossarrow silm:hasLongDescription "The IntegratedRepresentableCrossArrow is concretely, the cross-entity arrow exhibited in the section diagram, anchored in the household story. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'cross-entity arrow of section', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
